FULL = "filling this world and filling the next"
EN[4] = [
 f"{P} {M}, Your servant and Messenger, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of {M}.",
 f"{P} {FAM} with blessings that please You, reward him and fulfil his right. Give him the Wasilah, the excellence and the Praised Station You promised him; reward him on our behalf as he deserves, and with the best You have ever rewarded a prophet for his people and a messenger for his community; and send blessings upon all his brothers among the prophets and the righteous, O Most Merciful of the merciful.",
 f"O Allah, place the best of Your blessings, the noblest of Your purifications, Your growing graces and the tenderness of Your kindness, mercy and greeting, and the finest of Your favours, upon {M}, master of the Messengers, Messenger of the Lord of the worlds, leader to good, opener of righteousness, Prophet of mercy and master of the Ummah.",
 "O Allah, raise him to a praised station by which You bring him near, cool his eye, and for which the first and the last will long to share his place.",
 "O Allah, give him the bounty and the excellence, the honour and the Wasilah, the lofty rank and the towering station.",
 f"O Allah, give {M} the Wasilah, bring him what he hopes for, and make him the first to intercede and the first whose intercession is accepted.",
 "O Allah, make his proof great, make his Scales heavy, make his argument shine, and raise his rank among the people of 'Illiyyin,",
 "and his station among the highest of those brought near.",
 "O Allah, let us live upon his Sunnah and take our souls upon his religion,",
 "make us among the people of his intercession,",
 "gather us in his company, bring us to his Pool,",
 "and give us to drink from his cup, not disgraced, not regretful, not doubting, not altering, not changing, neither tempting others nor tempted. Amin, O Lord of the worlds.",
 f"{P} {FAM}, give him the Wasilah, the excellence and the lofty rank, and raise him to the Praised Station You promised him, together with his brothers the prophets.",
 f"May Allah send blessings upon {M}, the Prophet of mercy and master of the Ummah, and upon our father, our master Adam, and our mother, our lady Hawwa', and those of their children who were prophets, truthful, martyrs and righteous; and send blessings upon all Your angels among the people of the heavens and the earths, and upon us with them, O Most Merciful of the merciful.",
 "O Allah, forgive me my sins, and my parents, and have mercy on them as they raised me when I was small; and forgive all the believing men and women and the Muslim men and women, the living and the dead, and keep good things flowing between us and them. My Lord, forgive and have mercy, You are the best of those who show mercy.",
 "There is no power and no strength except by Allah, the High, the Mighty.",
 f"{P} {M}, the light of lights, the secret of secrets, the master of the righteous, the adornment of the chosen Messengers, the noblest of all on whom night has fallen and day has dawned, as many as the drops of rain from the beginning of the world to its end, and as many as the plants and trees that have grown from the beginning of the world to its end: blessings lasting as long as the kingdom of Allah, the One, the Irresistible.",
 f"{P} {M} with blessings by which You honour his resting place, ennoble his outcome and grant him his hopes and good pleasure on the Day of Resurrection.",
 "This blessing is in honour of your right, O our master Muhammad. (Three times)",
 f"{P} {M}: the Ha' of mercy, the Mim of sovereignty and the Dal of permanence; the perfect master, the opener and the seal; as many as all that is in Your knowledge, that is or has been, whenever those who remember mention You and him, and whenever the heedless forget to mention You and him:",
 "blessings lasting as You last and remaining as You remain, with no end short of Your knowledge. You have power over all things. (Three times)",
 f"{P} {M}, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of {M}, the brightest and most dazzling in light of all the suns of guidance,",
 "the most far-reaching and renowned of the prophets in honour,",
 "whose light is the most radiant, shining and clear of the prophets' lights,",
 "and who is the purest and cleanest of creation in character, and the noblest and most balanced in form.",
 f"{P} {M}, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of {M}, more beautiful than the full moon and more generous than the rain-bearing clouds and the vast ocean.",
 f"{P} {M}, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of {M}, with whose person and face blessing was joined, and by the fragrance of whose mention the worlds were perfumed.",
 f"{P} {M} and his family, and grant them peace.",
 f"{P} {FAM}; bless {FAM}; and have mercy upon {FAM}; as You sent blessings, grace and mercy upon our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 f"{P} {M}, Your servant, Prophet and Messenger, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of {M}.",
 f"{P} {FAM}, {FULL};",
 f"and bless {FAM}, {FULL};",
 f"and have mercy upon {FAM}, {FULL};",
 f"and reward {FAM}, {FULL};",
 f"and grant peace to {FAM}, {FULL}.",
 f"{P} {M} as You commanded us to send blessings upon him,",
 f"and send blessings upon {M} as blessings upon him should be sent.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon Your chosen Prophet, Your well-pleasing Messenger, Your elect friend, and Your trusted one over the revelation of heaven.",
 f"{P} {M}, the noblest of forebears, who upheld justice and fairness, described in Surat al-A'raf, chosen from the loins of noble men and fine wombs, purified from the pure line of 'Abd al-Muttalib son of 'Abd Manaf; by whom You guided out of dispute and made clear the way of chastity.",
 f"O Allah, I ask You by the best way of asking You, by the most beloved of Your names to You and the most honoured of them with You, and by the favour You did us through our master Muhammad, our Prophet ﷺ, by whom You rescued us from misguidance, commanding us to send blessings upon him and making our blessings upon him a rank, an expiation, a kindness and a gift from Your giving. So I call upon You in honour of Your command, following Your instruction and seeking Your promise, for what is due to our Prophet, our master Muhammad ﷺ, of his right over us, since we believed in him, affirmed him and followed the light sent down with him. And You said, and Your word is the truth: 'Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. O you who believe, send blessings upon him and greet him with abundant peace.'",
 f"You commanded Your servants to send blessings upon their Prophet as an obligation You laid upon them. So we ask You by the majesty of Your Face, the light of Your greatness, and what You have made binding upon Yourself for those who do good, that You and Your angels send blessings upon {M}, Your servant, Messenger, Prophet, chosen one and the best of Your creation, the best blessings You have ever sent upon anyone of Your creation. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, raise his rank, honour his station, make his Scales heavy, make his proof shine, make his religion prevail, make his reward abundant, make his light shine, make his honour last, join to him those of his descendants and the people of his house who will cool his eye, and make him great among the prophets who came before him.",
 f"O Allah, make {M} the prophet with the most followers and helpers, the best of them in honour and light,",
 "the highest of them in rank,",
 "and the most spacious of them in his home in Paradise.",
 "O Allah, place his goal among the foremost and his station among the chosen,",
 "his home among those brought near and his station among the elect.",
 "O Allah, make him the most honoured of the honoured with You in station, the best of them in reward, the nearest of them in sitting, the firmest of them in standing, the most right of them in speech, the most successful of them in asking, the best of them in share with You and the greatest of them in longing for what is with You,",
 "and bring him to the high chambers of al-Firdaws, among the loftiest ranks, above which there is no rank.",
 f"O Allah, make {M} the most truthful of speakers, the most successful of askers, the first to intercede and the best whose intercession is accepted. Accept his intercession for his Ummah with an intercession for which the first and the last will long to share his place. And when You separate Your servants with Your final judgement, place {M} among the most truthful in word, the best in deed and the most rightly guided in path.",
 "O Allah, make our Prophet go ahead of us to prepare our way, and make his Pool our meeting place, the first of us and the last.",
 "O Allah, gather us in his company, use us in his Sunnah, take our souls upon his religion, let us know his face, and place us among his company and his party.",
 "O Allah, bring us together with him, as we have believed in him without seeing him, and do not separate us from him until You enter us where he enters, bring us to his Pool and make us among his companions, with those You have blessed among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs and the righteous; and how excellent they are as companions.",
 "All praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds.",
 f"{P} {M}, the light of guidance, the leader to good, the caller to right guidance, the Prophet of mercy, the leader of the God-fearing and the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds, after whom there is no prophet; as he conveyed Your message, advised Your servants, recited Your verses, upheld Your limits, kept Your covenant, carried out Your judgement, commanded obedience to You and forbade disobedience to You, befriended Your friend whom You love to befriend and opposed Your enemy whom You love to oppose. May Allah send blessings upon {M}.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon his body among the bodies, his soul among the souls, his standing place among the standing places, his presence among the scenes of presence, and upon the mention of him whenever he is mentioned: a blessing from us upon our Prophet.",
 "O Allah, convey to him our greeting of peace, as peace has been mentioned. Peace be upon the Prophet, and the mercy of Allah Most High and His blessings.",
 "O Allah, send blessings upon Your angels brought near, Your purified prophets, Your sent messengers, the bearers of Your Throne, our master Jibril, our master Mika'il, our master Israfil, our master the Angel of Death, our master Ridwan the keeper of Your Garden, and our master Malik; send blessings upon the noble scribes, and upon all the people of obedience to You among the people of the heavens and the earths.",
 "O Allah, give the people of Your Prophet's house the best You have given any of the households of the Messengers, and reward the Companions of Your Prophet with the best You have rewarded any of the companions of the Messengers.",
 "O Allah, forgive the believing men and women and the Muslim men and women, the living and the dead,",
 "and forgive us and our brothers who went before us in faith, and leave no rancour in our hearts towards those who believe. Our Lord, You are Kind, Merciful.",
 f"O Allah, send blessings upon the Hashimi Prophet, {M}, and upon his family and Companions, and grant them abundant peace.",
 f"{P} {M}, the best of creation, with blessings that please You and please him, and by which You are pleased with us, O Most Merciful of the merciful.",
 f"{P} {M} and upon his family and Companions, and grant them peace, abundant, good, blessed, plentiful and beautiful, lasting as long as the kingdom of Allah.",
 f"{P} {M} and his family, filling all of space and as many as the stars in the sky, blessings equal in weight to the heavens and the earth, as many as all You have created and will create until the Day of Resurrection.",
 f"{P} {FAM}, as You sent blessings upon our master Ibrahim; and bless {FAM}, as You blessed our master Ibrahim and the family of our master Ibrahim among all the worlds. You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.",
 "O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in religion, in this world and in the next. (Three times)",
 "O Allah, cover us with Your beautiful covering. (Three times)",
 "O Allah, I ask You by Your mighty right, by the right of the light of Your noble Face, by the right of Your mighty Throne, by what Your Footstool carries of Your greatness, majesty, beauty, splendour, power and authority, and by the right of Your treasured and hidden names that none of Your creation has come to know.",
 "O Allah, I ask You by the name You placed upon the night and it grew dark, and upon the day and it grew bright,",
 "upon the heavens and they were raised,",
 "upon the earth and it was made firm,",
 "upon the mountains and they were anchored,",
 "upon the seas and valleys and they flowed,",
 "upon the springs and they gushed,",
 "and upon the clouds and they rained.",
 "And I ask You, O Allah, by the names written on the forehead of our master Israfil, peace be upon him, and by the names written on the forehead of our master Jibril, peace be upon him, and upon the angels brought near.",
 "And I ask You, O Allah, by the names written around the Throne and the names written around the Footstool.",
 "And I ask You, O Allah, by the name written on the olive leaf.",
 "And I ask You, O Allah, by the mighty names by which You have named Yourself, those I know and those I do not know.",
]

